late="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3500x1969+0+150/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F92%2F48%2Face884c742c6a37864ee16fd4434%2Fap26184135112797.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3500x1969+0+150/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F92%2F48%2Face884c742c6a37864ee16fd4434%2Fap26184135112797.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3500x1969+0+150/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F92%2F48%2Face884c742c6a37864ee16fd4434%2Fap26184135112797.jpg" class="img" alt="FILE PHOTO - A view outside Madison Square Garden from Seventh Avenue in New York." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 FILE PHOTO - A view outside Madison Square Garden from Seventh Avenue in New York.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Evan Agostini/AP Photo                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;New York City police are investigating after a video posted on social media captured another group of people &lt;a href="https://gothamist.com/news/another-group-of-people-spotted-emerging-from-an-nyc-manhole" target="_blank"&gt;emerging from a manhole&lt;/a&gt;. (via &lt;a href="https://gothamist.com/" target="_blank"&gt;Gothamist&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A recent drug bust at Penn State University linked to an alleged cocaine ring has drawn national attention to drug use on college campuses. But research shows that &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/08/24/nx-s1-5942987/cocaine-use-is-down-but-alcohol-is-still-being-abused-by-young-adults" target="_blank"&gt;alcohol poses a greater risk&lt;/a&gt; to students.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;At least 25% of former NFL players who participated in at least one game during their careers and died between 2016 and 2021 were found to have &lt;a href="http://npr.org/2026/08/25/nx-s1-5943168/cte-nfl-concussions-deaths-study" target="_blank"&gt;CTE upon their death&lt;/a&gt;, according to a new study from researchers at Mass General Brigham.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
